{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"344393de8d9a2378b3ecf99207c398d879228e61d18da8ff5731e34991239942","digest":{"component_or_area":"fetcher boundary / Cloud adapter enrichment","key_entities":["RunawayPaginationError","BackendPaginationStallError","adapters/jira/acli_graph.py","rebar_reconciler._backend","fetcher.fetch_snapshot","fetcher.py:621","fetcher.py:668","fetcher.py:708","get_parent_map","get_comment_map","get_issuelinks_map","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_graph_pagination_heldout.py"],"problem_keywords":["pagination stall","error swallowing","fail-open handler","type hierarchy","enrichment degradation","snapshot corruption"],"propositions":["RunawayPaginationError subclasses RuntimeError instead of BackendPaginationStallError, placing it outside the core stall type hierarchy","fetch_snapshot's three enrichment re-raise clauses match only on BackendPaginationStallError, so Cloud's RunawayPaginationError misses all three and falls through to the broad except Exception handlers","A stalled Cloud pagination cursor produces a silently degraded snapshot with missing parent/comment/issuelink data instead of aborting the pass","Making RunawayPaginationError subclass BackendPaginationStallError allows the three fetcher re-raise clauses to catch and propagate the stall, preserving all existing except clauses via MRO","Existing except RuntimeError sites remain unaffected because BackendPaginationStallError itself subclasses RuntimeError"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787647527779640682,"uuid":"ad38dfea-c621-4d1c-b6e2-083b54da05b3"}